---
// Static graphical method diagram for the worked example: the 2
// constraint lines, small arrows marking each half-space's feasible
// side, the shaded feasible region, and its 4 vertices.
---

<figure id="graphical-method-diagram">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 420 340" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img">
    <title>Graphical Method Worked Example</title>
    <defs>
      <marker
        id="gmd-arrow"
        viewBox="0 0 10 10"
        refX="8"
        refY="5"
        markerWidth="6"
        markerHeight="6"
        orient="auto-start-reverse"
      >
        <path
          d="M2 1L8 5L2 9"
          fill="none"
          stroke="context-stroke"
          stroke-width="1.5"
          stroke-linecap="round"
          stroke-linejoin="round"></path>
      </marker>
    </defs>

    <line class="axis" x1="50" y1="20" x2="50" y2="290"></line>
    <line class="axis" x1="50" y1="290" x2="390" y2="290"></line>
    <text class="axis-label" x="50" y="14" text-anchor="middle">x&#8322;</text>
    <text class="axis-label" x="390" y="315" text-anchor="end">x&#8321;</text>

    <polygon class="region" points="50,290 250,290 200,240 50,190"></polygon>

    <line class="curve c1" x1="50" y1="90" x2="250" y2="290"></line>
    <line class="curve c2" x1="50" y1="190" x2="350" y2="290"></line>

    <line
      class="halfplane-arrow c1"
      x1="150"
      y1="190"
      x2="137"
      y2="203"
      marker-end="url(#gmd-arrow)"></line>
    <line
      class="halfplane-arrow c2"
      x1="200"
      y1="240"
      x2="194"
      y2="257"
      marker-end="url(#gmd-arrow)"></line>

    <text class="curve-label c1" x="150" y="130">x&#8321; + x&#8322; = 4</text>
    <text class="curve-label c2" x="255" y="255">x&#8321; + 3x&#8322; = 6</text>

    <circle class="pt" cx="50" cy="290" r="5"></circle>
    <text class="pt-label" x="34" y="308">(0,0)</text>

    <circle class="pt" cx="250" cy="290" r="5"></circle>
    <text class="pt-label" x="234" y="308">(4,0)</text>

    <circle class="pt opt" cx="200" cy="240" r="5.5"></circle>
    <text class="pt-label" x="206" y="230">(3,1)</text>

    <circle class="pt" cx="50" cy="190" r="5"></circle>
    <text class="pt-label" x="14" y="185">(0,2)</text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>
    The feasible region is bounded by <span class="c1"
      >x&#8321; + x&#8322; &le; 4</span
    >,
    <span class="c2">x&#8321; + 3x&#8322; &le; 6</span>, and the axes. Arrows
    mark the feasible side of each constraint line. The optimal vertex
    <span class="opt">(3,1)</span> is where the 2 lines intersect.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  #graphical-method-diagram {
    max-width: 420px;
    margin: 24px auto;
  }

  #graphical-method-diagram svg {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  #graphical-method-diagram .axis {
    stroke: var(--text-muted);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }

  #graphical-method-diagram .axis-label {
    fill: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
  }

  #graphical-method-diagram .region {
    fill: var(--s5);
    fill-opacity: 0.15;
    stroke: none;
  }

  #graphical-method-diagram .curve {
    stroke-width: 2.5;
  }

  #graphical-method-diagram .curve.c1 {
    stroke: var(--s5);
  }

  #graphical-method-diagram .curve.c2 {
    stroke: var(--dia-ct);
  }

  #graphical-method-diagram .halfplane-arrow {
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }

  #graphical-method-diagram .halfplane-arrow.c1 {
    stroke: var(--s5);
  }

  #graphical-method-diagram .halfplane-arrow.c2 {
    stroke: var(--dia-ct);
  }

  #graphical-method-diagram .curve-label {
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  #graphical-method-diagram .curve-label.c1 {
    fill: var(--s5);
  }

  #graphical-method-diagram .curve-label.c2 {
    fill: var(--dia-ct);
  }

  #graphical-method-diagram .pt {
    fill: var(--text-primary);
    stroke: var(--surface);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }

  #graphical-method-diagram .pt.opt {
    fill: var(--dia-pt);
  }

  #graphical-method-diagram .pt-label {
    fill: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  #graphical-method-diagram figcaption {
    margin-top: 8px;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    text-align: center;
  }

  #graphical-method-diagram figcaption span {
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  #graphical-method-diagram figcaption .c1 {
    color: var(--s5);
  }

  #graphical-method-diagram figcaption .c2 {
    color: var(--dia-ct);
  }

  #graphical-method-diagram figcaption .opt {
    color: var(--dia-pt);
  }
</style>
